== Wake-Up and Saturation

#let wakeup = figure(
  caption: "Waking and saturating stumps.",
  box(width: 100%, stack(
    spacing: 18pt,
    subbox(caption: "Wake One Stump")[
      #flexbox(
        derive(
          "K-hit",
          ($(⟦S⟧ρ).l ↓ τ$, $S ⊢ δ ≐ τ ⇝ S′$),
          $S ⊢ ⟨α ⊳ ρ.l ↓ δ⟩ #st_wake S′ #st_drop ⟨α ⊳ ρ.l ↓ δ⟩$,
        ),
        derive(
          "K-⊥",
          ($(⟦S⟧ρ).l ↓ ⊥$, $S ⊢ δ ≐ ★ ⇝ S′$),
          $S ⊢ ⟨α ⊳ ρ.l ↓ δ⟩ #st_wake S′ #st_drop ⟨α ⊳ ρ.l ↓ δ⟩$,
        ),
        derive(
          "K-repark",
          ($(⟦S⟧ρ).l ↓ #h(0.2em) ? "on" α′$,),
          $S ⊢ ⟨α ⊳ ρ.l ↓ δ⟩ #st_wake (S #st_drop ⟨α ⊳ ρ.l ↓ δ⟩) #st_park ⟨α′ ⊳ ρ.l ↓ δ⟩$,
        ),
      )
    ],
    subbox(caption: "Saturate")[
      #flexbox(
        derive("K!-done", ($S "quiescent"$,), $S ⊢ Δ #st_sat S$),
        derive(
          "K!-step",
          (
            $⟨α ⊳ ρ.l ↓ δ⟩ ∈ Δ$,
            $¬(⟦S⟧ρ).l ↓ #h(0.2em) ? "on" α$,
            $S ⊢ ⟨α ⊳ ρ.l ↓ δ⟩ #st_wake S₁$,
            $S₁ ⊢ Δ₁ #st_sat S′$,
          ),
          $S ⊢ Δ #st_sat S′$,
        ),
      )
    ],
  )),
)
#wakeup <wakeup>

@wakeup gives the judgements for single wake-ups and saturation. The judgement $S ⊢ ⟨α ⊳ ρ.l ↓ δ⟩ #st_wake S′$ wakes a single stump and re-checks the lookup. The three rules match the three verdicts of a lookup. K-hit applies when the lookup hits a definite type: it drops the stump and unifies δ with the found type. K-⊥ drops the stump and pins δ to ★. K-repark moves the stump to the new blocker α′. The stability lemma of @lookup-metatheory makes this sound because a definite lookup never changes, even after further substitutions.

The saturation judgement $#st_sat$ works on the state until it is quiescent again: it picks a stale stump from Δ and runs wake-up $#st_wake$ on it. The first two premises of K!-step select the stump: it is parked, and its lookup is no longer blocked on the recorded α. The lookup may still be blocked on another variable, and then K-repark applies. The third premise wakes the stump, and the fourth continues on the new state. K!-done ends a run when no stump is stale.

